 {"id":"README-21","status":"in_progress","priority":"P4","type":"task","complexity":3,"title":"P4 \u2014 README:183-194 'Example tree from project.scl' is fabricated: project.scl declares neither @ref:speclang/auth nor @ref:speclang/database, and 3 of the block's 5 leaf paths do not exist","reasoning":"README health sweep 2026-11-16 (speclang-readme lane). Doc severity P4 per Bane ruling 2026-09-30 (policy, not an assessment of the finding's class).\n\nFINDING (accuracy \u2014 a fenced tree presented as project.scl's real structure):\nREADME.md:183 says 'Example tree from `project.scl` (Layer 0):' and is followed by a fenced block (README.md:184-194) claiming this shape:\n  project.scl -> @ref:speclang/core -> { @ref:speclang/auth -> specs/auth/implementation.spec.md, src/auth/handler.ts }\n                                   -> { @ref:speclang/database -> src/db/client.ts }\n  project.scl -> @ref:speclang/cascade -> specs/cascade-protocol.spec.md\n\nMeasured against the repo at HEAD (/home/kara/speclang, sweep of 2026-11-16):\n\n1. specs/project.scl declares id \"@northstar/speclang\" (line 2), layer 0 (line 4), and 24 @ref: entries at lines 124-146: core, daemon, agent-protocol, skills, pipeline, recovery, file-naming, test-specs, cascade, workflow, opencode, headers, directory-structure, tools, sqlite, dynamic-split, deployment, mcp, mcp-openapi-generation, mcp-openapi-generation-cli, mcp-daemon, git-history, symlinks.\n   $ grep -c \"@ref:\" specs/project.scl          -> 24\n   $ grep -nE \"@ref:speclang/(auth|database)\" specs/project.scl -> no matches\n   So two of the block's three @refs (speclang/auth, speclang/database) are NOT refs of project.scl, and 22 of its 23 real refs never appear in the \"example tree\".\n\n2. Three of the five leaf paths in the block do not exist:\n   $ for p in specs/auth/implementation.spec.md src/auth/handler.ts src/db/client.ts; do test -e \"$p\" || echo MISSING $p; done\n     MISSING specs/auth/implementation.spec.md\n     MISSING src/auth/handler.ts\n     MISSING src/db/client.ts\n   $ ls -d src/auth            -> ls: cannot access 'src/auth': No such file or directory\n   $ ls -d specs/auth*         -> specs/auth.spec.dir   specs/auth.spec.md    (no implementation.spec.md)\n   $ ls -la src/db             -> only symlinks index.ts, migrations.ts, poc-db.ts; no client.ts\n   The two paths that DO exist: specs/core.spec.md and specs/cascade-protocol.spec.md.\n\n3. Consequence: the section is titled 'Specs Define the Tree Structure' and the reader learns the layer model from a tree no file in the repo produces \u2014 the two example branches a newcomer is most likely to try (auth, database) lead to files that have never existed.\n\nRelated, deliberately NOT duplicated here: README-5 (README.md:348/:533 examples drift), README-9 (README.md:412-414 compile-health claims that mention src/auth), README-19 (spec counts). This row is scoped to README.md:183-194 only.\n\nFIX: replace the fenced block with a tree derived from project.scl's actual refs (or a small real subtree whose entries all resolve), and drop the auth/database/client.ts branch unless those files are created \u2014 or create the files the docs promise. Do not invent refs.\n\nPASS: 'sed -n \"184,194p\" README.md' piped through a per-path existence test prints no MISSING line, and any @ref: shown inside the block is present in specs/project.scl (grep -c for each >= 1); equivalently the block is replaced and 'grep -cE \"@ref:speclang/(auth|database)\" specs/project.scl' matches what the block shows.","acceptance_criteria":"The 'Example tree from project.scl' block is reconciled to output a reader can reproduce: the documented command that lists the project's spec tree from specs/project.scl exits 0, and every leaf path shown in the README block appears verbatim in that command's output (zero README leaves missing from it). Every `@ref:` identifier the block depicts is declared in specs/project.scl (grep -c on the spec file is >= 1 for each). If the tree cannot be produced from project.scl at all, the block is replaced by the honest generated output plus the exact command. Evidence: the command, its exit code, and the diff between block leaves and generated leaves.","detail":{"metadata":{},"fingerprint":"6c97744ad95f6723bf6810058ae106bcb8870602ea14ac47ecdbf74f5ff11ede"},"capability_tags":["docs","readme"],"created_at":"2026-11-16T10:58:06.437399+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-18T14:45:16.618398+00:00","worktree":"/home/kara/worktrees/SpecLang-README-21","branch":"wt/README-21","sessions":["SpecLang-foreman-2026-11-17-17-45-01"],"foreman_note":"Tick SpecLang-dogfood-2026-11-17-21-02-51: work MERGED at d6913213 and independently verified (23 refs in specs/project.scl == 23 in the block; all 24 printed paths exist; layer groups match each target spec header; auth/database refs gone). Judge evidence: run 27cb9590 FAILed only on a criterion whose reason was the literal string 'placeholder' (judge defect); retry run 44fd47b4 tier2 PASS but tier1 tests TIMED OUT after 120s (the known step-budget defect, documented by DF-SPECLANG-12), so Overall=FAIL-DEGRADED. Not closed: needs a judge run with a raised tier1 step budget.\n\nSpecLang-qa 13-57-02 independent re-verification: work MERGED at d6913213 (confirmed ancestor of origin/main). README block at origin/main:259-292 lists 23 @ref: identifiers, all 23 declared in specs/project.scl (0 missing), and all 23 arrow targets exist on disk (0 missing). RESIDUAL against this row's acceptance: the block does not print the exact command that reproduces the tree, so the first arm (documented command exits 0, every leaf in its output) is not literally provable as written. Row left in_progress for that reason \u2014 not closed."}
